Subject: keybind-v2: font smoothing scoped to the component

What: the sheet's universal rule (`* { -webkit-font-smoothing; -moz-osx-font-smoothing;
text-rendering }`) applies to `[data-component="keybind-v2"]` instead; all three
properties inherit, so the keys and labels keep them.
Why: a universal rule in a component sheet restyles every element on the page the
moment the component's module loads, and matches every element the style engine
resolves.

diff --git a/src/v2/components/keybind-v2.css b/src/v2/components/keybind-v2.css
index 5248476f73..2fcd7b1e81 100644
--- a/src/v2/components/keybind-v2.css
+++ b/src/v2/components/keybind-v2.css
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-* {
+[data-component="keybind-v2"] {
   -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
   -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
   text-rendering: geometricPrecision;
